{"id":"doc:docs/knowledge-crib-technical-pitch.md#how-it-works","kind":"doc-section","file":"docs/knowledge-crib-technical-pitch.md","heading":"How it works","level":2,"anchor":"how-it-works","span":{"start":15,"end":35},"lang":"markdown","hash":"blake3:6fac0428d75f658d74de4b41f8b3379b9a23a61cda8cbe7af5c42bc498e88e51","meta":{"codeRefs":["text\nRepository + docs\n  → structure map + language extractors\n  → cross-file resolution + CFG / SQL / framework passes\n  → doc-to-code links + clusters + ownership\n  → committed JSONL Soul (.crib/ node and edge shards)\n  → rebuildable SQLite FTS5 + adjacency index (.crib/index)\n  → bounded MCP tools / CLI / local graph UI","Two stores enforce clear trust boundaries:\n\n| Store | Role | Properties |\n|---|---|---|\n| **SoulStore** | Source of truth | Sharded JSONL, stable IDs and BLAKE3 hashes, schema validation, atomic writes, git-diffable, portable. |\n| **IndexStore** | Query acceleration | Derived SQLite FTS5, graph adjacency, source-body projection. Rebuildable; never source of truth. |\n\nEach graph edge carries relation, derivation method, provenance (","or","), confidence, and optional evidence. Consumers can request","Repository","docs","structure","map","language","extractors","cross","file","resolution","CFG","SQL","framework","passes","doc","to","code","links","clusters","ownership","committed","JSONL","Soul",".crib/","node","and","edge","shards","rebuildable","SQLite","FTS5","adjacency","index",".crib/index","bounded","MCP","tools","CLI","local","graph","UI"],"links":[]}}
